00:21:07,430 --> 00:21:11,190
a user instruction, it would not have worked.

284
00:21:11,190 --> 00:21:13,270
So, the premise being if it comes through an indirect source,

285
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:19,430
the LLM gets confused whether that's a user instruction or a system instruction.

286
00:21:19,430 --> 00:21:21,910
The instructions could have come directly from the user itself.

287
00:21:21,910 --> 00:21:27,870
But in that case, the attacker would have to trigger the attack by directly instructing Copilot.

