00:23:03,750 --> 00:23:12,751
I mean, 330,000 prompts consisting of more than 330 million tokens from participants coming from more than 80. countries.

313
00:23:12,751 --> 00:23:17,590
So, it really opened our eyes to the creative techniques.

314
00:23:17,590 --> 00:23:21,910
that the attackers use in order to attack the system and so on and so forth.

315
00:23:21,910 --> 00:23:24,550
So, the game was really comprised you know.

316
00:23:24,550 --> 00:23:29,990
followed an escape room theme where users are expected to jump from room one to room two to.

317
00:23:29,990 --> 00:23:32,110
room with increasing levels of difficulties.

318
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:35,150
and they are supposed to solve the challenge.

319
00:23:35,150 --> 00:23:39,630
and the challenge answer really is the key to enter the next room.

320
00:23:39,630 --> 00:23:41,830
So, all the three system rooms had different levels of difficulties.

321
00:23:41,830 --> 00:23:45,790
The first room simply was about system prompt guardrails.

322
00:23:45,790 --> 00:23:49,510
So, system prompt in itself contained all the guardrails.

323
00:23:49,510 --> 00:23:51,950
and said what to do and what not to do.

324
00:23:51,950 --> 00:23:56,550
Here in this case, the system prompt actually contained the secret.

325
00:23:56,550 --> 00:24:01,150
that was the objective of the challenge to retrieve the secret.

326
00:24:01,150 --> 00:24:03,550
and the system prompt itself had instructions on the fact.

327
00:24:03,550 --> 00:24:05,630
that the secret should not be revealed etc. etc.

328
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:09,110
So, the guardrails were part of the system prompt.

329
00:24:09,110 --> 00:24:16,910
which is typically the design of most generative AI applications when they're written to start with.

330
00:24:16,910 --> 00:24:21,510
Now, the second room or the second level was about of course the system prompt guardrails.

331
00:24:21,510 --> 00:24:23,710
but now we added input.

