00:29:47,990 --> 00:29:50,030
So, a lot of good learnings for us.

401
00:29:50,030 --> 00:29:55,630
and we were able to incorporate all of those learnings into the next level of protection techniques. that we rolled into our product.

402
00:29:55,640 --> 00:30:00,030
So, you mentioned about ingress and egress.

403
00:30:00,030 --> 00:30:02,430
But, what does it mean and how is it used in an attack?

404
00:30:02,440 --> 00:30:04,430
Yeah.

405
00:30:04,430 --> 00:30:08,310
In case of interacting with an LLM, the data is sent to the LLM,

406
00:30:08,310 --> 00:30:12,830
and the output of the LLM is sent back to the user.

407
00:30:12,830 --> 00:30:15,790
So, when I talk about these filters,

408
00:30:15,790 --> 00:30:19,230
you can apply the filters on what the user is entering into the prompt.

409
00:30:19,240 --> 00:30:24,230
And again, filters can be applied on contextual data.

410
00:30:24,230 --> 00:30:28,030
that is pulled in in relation to to the user question before it is sent to the LLM.

411
00:30:28,030 --> 00:30:32,390
So, you can apply the filters on the data just before the data is sent to the LLM.

412
00:30:32,390 --> 00:30:40,071
Therein, you can say things like, "This is an application which only serves the needs of English-speaking users. Thereby.

413
00:30:40,071 --> 00:30:44,550
any other language should not be allowed on this generative AI application.

414
00:30:44,550 --> 00:30:46,350
So, you can put in language filters.

415
00:30:46,350 --> 00:30:51,750
You can deny usage of any other language other than English because again,

416
00:30:51,750 --> 00:30:59,630
the attacks because the LLMs are so good, they can understand instructions in any and all formats.

