00:31:08,150 --> 00:31:10,830
they would not be able to detect malicious tokens in other languages.

420
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:14,950
So, when we are talking about ingress filters,

421
00:31:14,950 --> 00:31:21,190
we're talking about protection techniques that have been put in on the data that goes to the LLM.

422
00:31:21,190 --> 00:31:23,390
And once the data has been sent to the LLM,

423
00:31:23,400 --> 00:31:27,710
provided that it is allowed because of the ingress filters.

424
00:31:27,710 --> 00:31:29,910
when the data comes out of the LLM,

425
00:31:29,910 --> 00:31:31,550
you can then again inspect the data to make sure.

426
00:31:31,550 --> 00:31:36,190
that it does not have any kind of malicious tokens.

427
00:31:36,190 --> 00:31:40,990
or unexpected things and so on so forth in order to lower the risk of information accidental.

428
00:31:40,990 --> 00:31:42,990
or deliberate leakage back to the user.

429
00:31:42,990 --> 00:31:50,110
So, for example, if I'm extremely concerned about ever leaking social security numbers,

430
00:31:50,110 --> 00:31:54,790
I can put in egress filter to detect a pattern of numbers which represent.

431
00:31:54,790 --> 00:31:57,390
or look like social security and if I see that anywhere,

432
00:31:57,390 --> 00:32:01,190
I can decide to redact or block the data from going back to the user.

433
00:32:01,200 --> 00:32:05,430
So, those are the two kinds of filters that can be put in place.

434
00:32:05,430 --> 00:32:07,630
And in case of the game that we had designed.

